VIEWMODEL.md §3.5, log-2026-09-28 U5 review calls: a `step` text using anything but a bare `{index}` is E1623: another name, an expression, a format spec; a bare `{index}` beside them is fine.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Item {
  level: Int
  steps: [Int]
  rungs: [Int]
  ranks: [Int]
  tiers: [Int]
}

view Item {
  steps { step: "Step {index} of {level}" }
  rungs { step: "Rung {index + 1}" }
  ranks { step: "Rank {index:,}" }
  tiers { step: "Tier {index}" }
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E1623]  a/a.canon:12:35
  a step text may only use {index}, not {level}

error[E1623]  a/a.canon:13:24
  a step text may only use {index}, not {index + 1}

error[E1623]  a/a.canon:14:24
  a step text may only use {index}, not {index:,}

